ported only on short cycles. The restrictions of the trivial and sign characters to the cyclic subgroup evaluate the constants exactly, whereas a uniform binomial contraction controls every distance from the boundary at once. If neither a row nor a column has a majority, Swanson's opposite-hook estimate gives a Catalan-scale lower bound for the dimension. The Fomin--Lulov rectangular-character estimate, together with uniform bounds for the truncated Möbius weights, then shows that the identity class dominates. Sundaram's plethystic identity consequently implies that $\\prod_{r=1}^M(1-p_r)^{-1}$ is Schur-positive for every fixed $M$. We also record a degree-$12$ counterexample to a separate congruence-class product conjecture attributed to Richard Stanley.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nlattice — arXiv Combinatorics (https://arxiv.symmetricfunctions.com/keyword/lattice?page=4)\nciteturn1search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Recently, Ferroni constructed a family of counterexamples to the well-known conjecture in Ehrhart theory stating that the $h^*$-polynomial of a lattice polytope with the integer decomposition property is unimodal. ... We prove the covering property for every parallelepiped containing five vertices of $Q_3$, and, in any dimension, for every parallelotope containing a facet of $Q_n$ and one vertex of the opposite facet. ... We also give an alternative proof of this bound.\npolynomial lattice\n\n2026-10-14\n\nYang Li, San Ling, Zhonghua Sun, Shixin Zhu\n\n# • INFO • BIB • PDF • ARXIV •\n\nProofs and disproofs of some conjectures on zero-sum problems of new types\n\nFor integers $r\\ge1$ and $n\\ge2$, let $s_r(n)$ be the least $N$ such that every sequence of $N$ vectors in $\\Z^r$, each nonzero modulo $n$, contains $n$ terms whose sum is zero modulo $n$ but nonzero modulo $n^2$. Let $w_r(n)$ be the corresponding least $N$ when any nonempty subsequence is allowed. These constants were introduced as 